{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"Joseph's brothers have come\"</b> is that Joseph had made known to Pharaoh's household that he has honorable brothers in the land of the Hebrews, for he was stolen away from there, and now they heard that Joseph's brothers had come, as it says:" "<b>\"And it was pleasing in the eyes of Pharaoh and in the eyes of his servants\"</b>, because the matter had been to them a disgrace that a foreigner should rule over them, a slave who came out of the house of bondage to become king, and now that honorable brothers had come to him and it became known that he is fit to stand before kings, they all rejoiced in the matter:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:58.308453127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}